# Ignore dataset artifacts and generated data
data/*.csv
data/*.zip
data/*.pkl
data/models_pretrained/
data/data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
logs/

# Exceptions: small, deliverable files worth tracking despite the blanket
# rules above. Raw source data (csic_database.csv, labeled_csic_database.csv,
# Attack_Dataset.csv, XSS_dataset.csv — license/terms of use unverified, see
# docs/DATASET.md), in-progress backup snapshots (augmented_web_attack_PRE_*.csv),
# the 321MB web_graphs.pkl (regenerable via scripts/build_graphs.py, would
# exceed GitHub's 100MB file limit), and test_split_indices_SQLI_ONLY_bug.pkl
# (obsolete artifact of a fixed bug) stay ignored.
!data/augmented_web_attack.csv
!data/sqli_payload_pool.csv
!data/heldout_keyword_test.csv
!data/test_split_indices.pkl
!data/sqli_family_test_indices.pkl

# External evaluation dataset (Reviewer #1: independent public dataset,
# evaluation-only, MIT-licensed -- see docs/DATASET.md "External Evaluation
# Dataset"). Explicit even though `data/*.csv`/`data/*.pkl` above are
# single-level globs that don't currently reach data/external/ -- this
# future-proofs against the blanket rule ever becoming recursive.
!data/external/*.csv
# external_dataset_graphs.pkl (155MB, regenerable via
# scripts/build_external_graphs.py from external_dataset_clean.csv) stays
# ignored -- exceeds GitHub's 100MB hard file-size limit, same reasoning as
# the top-level web_graphs.pkl exclusion above.
data/external/*.pkl

# Transformer baseline train/test text CSVs (Reviewer #3 baselines) --
# regenerable in seconds via scripts/prepare_transformer_baseline_data.py
# from the already-frozen augmented_web_attack.csv/test_split_indices.pkl,
# same reasoning as web_graphs.pkl above.
data/transformer_baseline/
